{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776027382,"nonce":"oRhpbqwIOrGZWSuRKsubamqhfL0=","title":"Post-merge: offer to remove feature worktree and branch","message":"After a successful auth merge, the feature worktree and branch are no longer needed. Mandible should either:\n\n1. **Automatically remove** the worktree and branch after a successful merge (with a confirmation prompt in the dashboard), or\n2. **Offer a one-click option** in the auth result notification to clean up the worktree\n\nCurrently the user must manually run `dwt \u003cbranch\u003e` after every merge, which is easy to forget and leaves stale worktrees accumulating.\n\nThe cleanup should:\n- Run `dwt \u003cbranch\u003e` (which handles cwd safety and untracked-file checks)\n- Delete the local branch ref if fully merged\n- Report what was cleaned in the auth result output\n\nEdge case: if the worktree has untracked files or uncommitted changes (e.g. font cache artifacts from renders), prompt before force-removing rather than silently failing.","files":null}]}